    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Part U §2, Chap 56 of 2018",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9129\n\nSPONSOR: GOUNARDES\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend part U of chapter 56 of the laws of 2018, amending the\neducation law relating to requiring regulations to permit tuition waiv-\ners for certain firefighters and fire officers for CUNY, in relation to\nthe effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo purpose of this bill is to extend the law that provides certain fire-\nfighters and fire officers enrolled at CUNY with a tuition waiver for\none course.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill amends chapter 56 of the laws of 2018 to extend\nthe law for an additional two years to July 1, 2024.\n\nSection two of the bill provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill provides an incentive for firefighters and fire officers to\npursue higher education by authorizing a tuition wavier for one course\nat CUNY.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter 58 of the Laws of 2020 (Item LL of subpart B of Part XXX)\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
